      {
        "id": 86227,
        "name": "danmarshall14",
        "username": "danmarshall14",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/danmarshall14/{size}/1944_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-01-10T14:37:58.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Think of it this way; anything that does not say \"One-Shot\" stays on the field; this can include Ongoings, Equipment, Components, Relics, Modes, and many are combinations of such.&nbsp; Anything that destroys&nbsp;these will specify&nbsp;in the card text.&nbsp; If&nbsp;a villain card says \"destroy an Equipment Card\" or one of Omnitron-X's cards say \"Destroy a Component card\", Omni-X's Innervation Ray can be destroyed by either as it's title is \"Equipment,&nbsp;Component\".</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Any card that has Ongoing in the title can be destroyed by Ongoing destruction; anything with Equipment in the title can be destroyed by Equipment destruction.&nbsp; In the end, it all comes down to the text of the card.</p>",
        "post_number": 6,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:10:09.407Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 0,
